+      <p class="agent-note">Agent: I would explain my diff, but you would have to read it.</p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
+      <div class="section-heading">
+        <p class="eyebrow">Shared view</p>
+        <h2 id="future-heading">Our take on AI and the future of software engineering</h2>
+        <p class="section-intro">A few things we think matter, even as the tools change.</p>
+        <p class="microcopy">We asked an AI to predict the future. It said “it depends”.</p>
+        <p class="agent-note">Agent: I did not break it. I refactored it.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="belief-list" aria-label="Team beliefs">
+        <details open>
+          <summary>First drafts are cheap; judgement is the bottleneck.</summary>
+          <p>Generated code is a starting point. Engineers still need to decide whether it is correct, useful, and reliable.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details>
+          <summary>Prompting is not engineering.</summary>
+          <p>Understanding systems, architecture, security, and failure modes is how we use AI well and evaluate what it produces.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details>
+          <summary>Humans stay accountable.</summary>
+          <p>“The AI did it” is not an incident report. People remain responsible for the systems they ship.</p>
+        </details>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="disagreement">
+        <h3>Where we disagree</h3>
+        <pre class="stack-trace"><code>Exception: OpinionConflict at optimists.js:10 caused by sceptics.js:42</code></pre>
+        <button id="opinion-toggle" class="opinion-switch" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="opinion-copy">Show the optimists’ case</button>
+        <p id="opinion-copy" class="opinion" hidden><strong>Sceptics:</strong> Mostly yes—people will still hand-write most code, because deciding what to build is the hard part.</p>
+        <p class="disagreement-footer">We agree to disagree, then ask the agent to write a test for both opinions. Both pass. Suspicious.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
